course: dictionary
lesson: 5124
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word invasion has more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one. In a history story, «Viking invasions» means armies from another land attacking and taking over a place. At a picnic, «an invasion of wasps» means a large crowd of wasps arriving and spreading everywhere.
explain: Read the clues. Is there an army, a country or a fight? Then it means an army entering by force. Are there lots of animals, insects or things arriving? Then it means a large number arriving and spreading. Is someone's private space being entered without permission? Then it is the third meaning, as in «an invasion of privacy».
explain: Use the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense. «The wasps' invasion ruined our picnic» works, because a crowd of wasps can ruin a picnic. An army of soldiers would not fit into a picnic story at all.
explain: Invasion is also used in science. An invasive species is a plant or animal that spreads into a new place and can harm the wildlife that already lives there. Invasive is built from the same root as invasion, so the two words are closely linked.
fact: Invasion is a noun: an invasion, invasions.
fact: «Invasion» can mean an army entering another country by force to attack or take it.
fact: «Invasion» can also mean a large number of people, animals or things arriving and spreading somewhere, often causing trouble.
fact: «Invasion of privacy» means getting into something that should be private.
fact: Phrases such as «launch an invasion», «alien invasion» and «invasive species» show how the word is used.
exercise: «After Russia's full-scale invasion in 2022, millions of Ukrainians fled.» What does invasion mean here? | *An army entering another country by force | A kind of school trip | A crowd of tourists at a museum | A large party with lots of guests
exercise: «There was an invasion of wasps at our picnic.» What does invasion mean here? | Being very quiet and still | A type of sandwich | *A large number of wasps arriving and spreading | An army attacking a castle
exercise: Which phrase means getting into something that should be private? | alien invasion | launch an invasion | invasive species | *invasion of privacy
test: «The Romans made an invasion of Britain long ago.» Which meaning fits best? | *An army entering another land by force | A large crowd of tourists at a museum | Getting into a private diary | A tasty cake shared at a party
test: Scientists warn that an invasive species can harm local wildlife. What is an invasive species? | A small fish that lives in fresh water only | *A plant or animal that spreads into a new place and harms the wildlife there | A plant that grows only in deserts | A rare animal kept safe in a zoo
exam: Someone reads your private diary without asking. Which phrase fits best? | invasive species | invasion of wasps | Viking invasion | *invasion of privacy
